  "raw_text": "after all my work's done. No time pressure usually, just kind of after relaxing after the work's over. Agent: That's helpful to know. So, typically at night, by yourself, after work, and without time pressure. How does price change your choice? For example, if your Double Quarter Pounder with Cheese cost two dollars more, what would you do? User: I think I would still maybe I might go somewhere else if it costs a little more. Agent: Understood. So a two-dollar price increase might make you consider other options. What if there was a deal on the Double Quarter Pounder with Cheese? What would you do differently then? User: If there was a deal, then yeah, I'd still consider it depending on what I'm getting extra out of it. Agent: Okay, so a deal would definitely influence your choice, depending on what extra you'd get from it. Let's shift gears a bit. What does \"good value\" mean to you in fast food? Could you pick your top two or three factors, such as taste, portion size, speed, nutr",
